course: dictionary
lesson: 9671
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and success is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask yourself what kind of success the sentence is about.
explain: «Our class play was a success.» Here a success is something that went well. Check by swapping in "something that went well": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Practice is the key to success.» Here success means doing what you wanted or tried to do. The word «key» and the word «practice» are your clues.
fact: Success is a noun, so it names an idea or a thing.
fact: Success means doing what you wanted or tried to do.
fact: A success is something that goes well or works, as in «a great success».
fact: Success can also mean being famous, rich or doing well in life.
fact: «Someone else's success does not take anything away from you.»
exercise: «Our school play was a great success.» What does success mean here? | A sad feeling after a loss | *Something that went well | A tiny mistake | Being famous on television
exercise: «Finishing the puzzle on my own felt like success.» Which meaning fits? | Being rich | Something broken | A group of friends | *Doing what I tried to do
exercise: Which phrase from the lessons is about the secret to doing well? | a bright red ball | the key to the door | a cold wind | *the key to success
test: «With hard work, she reached success in her swimming.» What does success mean? | Going to bed early | *Doing what she tried to do | A quiet pool | Being lost
test: «Being happy for a friend's success is a skill that gets easier with practice.» What does this sentence tell us? | Success is always a bad thing | Practice takes away success | *Being glad for others gets easier with practice | Friends never have success
exam: «Someone else's success does not take anything away from you.» What is the best meaning of this sentence? | Your friend's win means you lose out | Success is only for famous people | *Another person doing well does not make you lose anything | Success always means someone else fails
